<title>USA: U.S. House tax chair - no stance on cigarette tax.</title>
<headline>U.S. House tax chair - no stance on cigarette tax.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>House Ways and Means Committee Chairman Bill Archer said Friday he was not going to take a position on a cigarette tax increase approved by the Senate Finance Committee, and that the issue would be dealt with in conference.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm not going to take a position on it,&quot; the Texas Republican told reporters. &quot;It's not in our House bill, we'll deal with it in conference.&quot;</p>
<p>The Senate Finance Committee late Thursday approved a tax bill that included a cigarette tax increase of 20 cents per pack that would be in addition to the current tax of 24 cents.</p>
</text>
